Workspace_DGO: canonical source review and release decision
=========================================================

Recommendation: NO-GO for public distribution or production release.
Review date: 2026-10-24. Default branch: workspace-source.
Canonical source for subsequent reviewed changes: Repo_root/.

This is a source-review baseline, NOT a complete or commissioned deployment.
Repository metadata describes a public repository, while the inherited README
says it must remain private. Treat that conflict as an exposure incident requiring
owner action, not permission to publish. No tenant was contacted, credentials
rotated, mail sent, deployment performed, or application package generated here.

Selection evidence
------------------
The comparison used actual git-tracked files, package scripts, source modules and
SHA-256 content equality, not version labels or inherited readiness assertions.
Counts below describe the snapshots at review start. "Tests" counts all tracked
files under tests/, including fixtures; it is NOT measured test coverage.

Candidate                                 Files  Core JS  Tests  npm scripts
Repo_root                                   791       96    179          352
ECM_DOCS_DEV-4e3efeaa211b97ee66d97af91ceac43519c0370e
                                            791       96    179          352
NITDA-Folio-Source-31e80475                   774       83    164          349
Commissioning-claude-isolated-code-session-scope-bghduo
                                            510       73    111          260
Folio-Workspace-Premium (1)                  214       83      0            0
runtime_folio-platform-suite-1.0.2           217       83      0            0
runtime_folio-platform-suite-1.0.3           237       96      0            0
Rationalisation_pack                          8        0      1          353

* Repo_root and ECM_DOCS_DEV had identical relative path sets and identical bytes
  for every one of their 791 files. Repo_root is selected for its clear path and
  stronger available source/test surface, not because it is called 1.0.3.
* Compared with Repo_root, NITDA-Folio-Source lacks 13 core modules, including
  record-view, record-search, inbox-view, overview, task-views and record-actions.
  Commissioning lacks 23, and has fewer scripts/tests and a session-scoped brief.
  Neither provides evidence of a more complete or more secure replacement.
* Premium and the runtime directories are useful visual/deployment references,
  not independently reproducible source baselines: no tracked test/tooling tree.
  Other redesign/upload snapshots are retained as references, not selected sources.
* Rationalisation_pack is an eight-file overlay, not a complete application.
  Its declared scripts depend on a larger tree. Module-boundary rationalisation
  is a possible future port, only after its dependencies, imports and dedicated
  tests are validated against this baseline. It is not integrated or certified.
* No snapshot was deleted or wholesale merged. There is no enhancement to port
  from an identical duplicate. Missing documents/portal files must be recovered
  from an owner-verified source, not guessed from a similarly named deployment.
  The authorised pinned recovery below now supplies the portal and selected inputs;
  the table above remains the initial-review comparison, not current file counts.

Repo_root/CLAUDE.md:3-18 mandates a claude branch and forbids PRs. That is a copied
workflow from another repository, not the workflow for Workspace_DGO. Work stays
on this task's review branch, targeting workspace-source. Its generated-file
guidance remains useful, but its closure records and "full gate" claims cannot
override missing files or fresh evidence in this repository.

Bounded improvements
--------------------
* A dependency-free root npm entry point selects Repo_root explicitly, runs an
  allowlist of existing offline checks, continues after failures, and reports
  statuses without printing raw child logs or secret values.
* The import checker now keeps recursive regex iteration independent, rejects
  missing HTML/module entry points, and resolves browser query/fragment suffixes.
  Four fixture regressions test these cases.
* Six gate tests cover redaction-by-design, tracked-only scanning, config and
  container blockers, subprocess failures/timeouts, real CLI mode dispatch in
  a throwaway repository and mandatory human gates.
* A separate two-test Playwright configuration verifies local boot and blocked
  remote requests. It ignores inherited remote-base settings, uses loopback only,
  substitutes empty local config, blocks non-GET/HEAD requests and WebSockets,
  disables service workers and does not record traces/screenshots/video.
* The inherited application README now points here before its stale claims.
  Build/dependency/browser output and new private config are ignored at repository
  root. Ignore rules do not remove or protect already tracked sensitive files.

Authorised selective recovery (2026-10-24)
------------------------------------------
The owner supplied dgoeaa/ECM_DOCS_DEV and explicitly authorised selective recovery
from commit 525fc666760726a1ca6fc23fd830782981f79419, excluding credentials and signed
endpoints. recovery-manifest.json records the source, scope, byte sizes and SHA-256
hashes. No source repository was cloned and no upstream scripts were executed.
Specific pinned files were staged outside the repository, screened, then copied
only to previously absent paths under Repo_root/. Existing source and assertions
were not overwritten, and the local improved import checker was retained.

Recovered: 37 portal runtime/page/design-system files; the essentials architecture
JSON and its existing generated document; the large-file governance record; one
scan-intake fixture needed by test:auth; and the portal-vault contract needed by
test:portalvault. Forty files match the pinned source exactly. The two flow test
inputs are deliberately sanitised and MUST NOT be deployed or used to commission:

* The scan fixture has its entire allConnectionData removed (deployment bindings),
  22 tenant-site URL occurrences replaced with an example.invalid address, and
  105 distinct GUID literals replaced one-to-one with synthetic identifiers.
* The portal-vault contract has 38 distinct GUID literals replaced with synthetic
  identifiers. Its endpoint aliases and other contract logic are preserved.
* The manifest records original and sanitised hashes, plus source-graph hashes
  normalised only for the declared configuration transformations. Regression
  tests confirm preservation of that graph, sanitisation, asset resolution,
  the pinned recovery boundary and every restored file's final bytes.

Not imported: private/local configuration, signed endpoints, tenant evidence,
reference archives, unrelated docs, deployment settings, upstream branch mandates,
or remaining flow packages. No package builder, flow generator or live check ran.
Source licence was compared and matches the existing licence.
Copied historical approval/closure records describe upstream, not new acceptance
or production-readiness evidence for Workspace_DGO. Their unresolved references
remain visible rather than being removed or accepted into a new baseline.

Recovery verification (Node v22.23.3, npm 10.9.9, /usr/bin/chromium):
  npm run test:gate                 PASS: 16 tests (10 existing + 6 recovery)
  npm run verify:offline           FAIL: 11 scripts pass, 3 fail
  npm test                         FAIL: regression tests pass; existing gates fail
  Repo_root/test:offline-browser    PASS: 3 tests, including all six portal pages
  Repo_root/npm ci (safe flags)     PASS: unchanged lockfile; lifecycle scripts off
  npm run audit:tracked            FAIL: unchanged 55 affected files (33 credential
                                  patterns, 21 containers, 1 config filename)

Now passing after recovery: assetstamp, uxplan, portaloutbox, portalvault, encoding
and auth. Auth's inert and enforced unit postures pass; that does NOT enable auth
in the application or prove any deployed tenant validates identities.

Remaining failures:
* test:hygiene: upstream baselines/approval records refer to absent reference
  artifacts; duplicate groups differ in this partial tree, and governance records
  remain missing. The historical approval list is not a local release approval.
* test:refs: the partial reference/docs tree still has unresolved relative links.
* test:node: stops at hygiene; later it also references undefined test:effectivity
  and test:constraints. These definitions are absent upstream too; no passing
  stubs, removed checks or acceptance-baseline regeneration were introduced.

Release remains NO-GO. Source recovery is not credential revocation, full-history
remediation, tenant authorisation, commissioning, rollback approval or owner signoff.
Initial-review evidence below is preserved as history, not the current failure list.

Reproduce safely
----------------
Use a disposable, restricted checkout. Do not supply tenant credentials or private
configuration. Do not serve the repository root or use inherited live, wiring,
commissioning or packaging commands. These commands use absolute paths for this
checkout; change the checkout prefix if reviewing elsewhere.

  cd /home/runner/work/Workspace_DGO/Workspace_DGO
  node --version
  npm --version
  npm run test:gate
  npm run verify:offline
  npm run audit:tracked
  npm run release:check

Node 22+ and npm are required. The root has no dependencies and needs no install.
Root npm test runs test:gate followed by verify:offline. Nonzero verification,
audit and release exits are intentional when findings/failures remain; do not
replace them with success or skip failing checks to obtain approval.

Optional isolated browser verification, using the existing locked dependencies:

  npm --prefix /home/runner/work/Workspace_DGO/Workspace_DGO/Repo_root ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
  PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/usr/bin/chromium npm --prefix /home/runner/work/Workspace_DGO/Workspace_DGO/Repo_root run test:offline-browser

The Chromium executable must exist (or omit that variable when Playwright's
matching browser is already installed). Port 18080 must be free. The server binds
only 127.0.0.1 and refuses to reuse an existing server. Do not use the inherited
remote-capable test:smoke command for this offline review. Browser dependencies
are installed without lifecycle scripts; nothing is packaged.
Browser tests are a separate explicit step, not part of verify:offline, which
remains dependency-free. Release acceptance requires both; a Node pass alone
cannot replace the isolated browser or externally authorised commissioning gates.

